# Transcaty Scope and Safety

- Build only what supports payment processing, wallet ledgering, merchant/provider auth, KYC gating, billing, and auditability.
- Do not add unrelated product features (CRM, chat, marketing, analytics-only work) unless explicitly requested.
- Any change touching money, auth, webhook verification, or provider admin controls must preserve backward-safe behavior.
- Prefer fail-safe outcomes: reject request or mark transaction failed instead of guessing success.
- Never remove or bypass signature checks, idempotency checks, balance checks, or role checks.
- Keep PII/secret exposure minimal: do not log plaintext secrets, API keys, tokens, or decrypted credential values.

## Out of Scope Guard

- If a request expands scope, propose a phased plan and implement only the approved phase.
- If security and feature speed conflict, prioritize security and explicit approval before weakening controls.
